WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.237 --> 00:00:02.499
- Just look at her hands and my hands,

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:04.217
that's the difference here.

00:00:04.217 --> 00:00:06.217
(drums)

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.233
- I've been making cakes for 8 years.

00:00:09.233 --> 00:00:10.441
How is this a contest?

00:00:10.441 --> 00:00:12.319
- Well, Bree has the techniques,

00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:14.296
but does she have the creativity?

00:00:14.296 --> 00:00:16.129
I don't think so.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.081
- I am a professional cake decorator

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:21.160
and owner of Bree's Cakes
here in Los Angeles.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.054
- I've maybe made like 3 cakes in my life.

00:00:24.054 --> 00:00:25.676
I have been drawing my whole life.

00:00:25.676 --> 00:00:27.731
I don't feel as confident I think.

00:00:27.731 --> 00:00:30.220
At least the colors will be nice.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.410
- I feel really confident about this

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.598
cause I do this everyday.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.431
- Hi-five.

00:00:33.431 --> 00:00:34.264
(squeals)

00:00:34.264 --> 00:00:36.181
Let's do this.
- Alright.

00:00:37.148 --> 00:00:38.407
- Wait, there are rules?

00:00:38.407 --> 00:00:40.115
- What kind of rules?

00:00:40.115 --> 00:00:40.951
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:00:40.951 --> 00:00:44.377
That's necessary.
- That's doable.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.210
- Okay.

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:50.921
(suspenseful music)

00:00:50.921 --> 00:00:52.073
Oh.
- Oh.

00:00:52.073 --> 00:00:53.293
Okay.
- Okay good.

00:00:53.293 --> 00:00:55.335
So I decided for my Sweet Sixteen cake

00:00:55.335 --> 00:00:58.950
to do very vibrant colors
cause if I was 16 again,

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.273
I'd want bright colors like
pink and purple and blue.

00:01:02.273 --> 00:01:03.429
So I'm gonna take all those colors

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:04.741
and make a striped buttercream

00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:07.026
and then top it with a fondant bow.

00:01:07.026 --> 00:01:09.281
- So today I'm gonna be
making a cake inspired

00:01:09.281 --> 00:01:11.380
by my favorite book, The Little Prince,

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.464
and I'm gonna make the
cake look like a meteor,

00:01:13.464 --> 00:01:16.263
then I'm gonna make a little
rose made out of fondant.

00:01:16.263 --> 00:01:17.625
It's gonna be great.

00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:19.239
- It's not as easy as it looks, is it?

00:01:19.239 --> 00:01:20.072
- Oh, no.

00:01:20.072 --> 00:01:21.186
Awful.

00:01:21.186 --> 00:01:22.223
Oh no.

00:01:22.223 --> 00:01:23.727
Are you supposed to knead it like this?

00:01:23.727 --> 00:01:24.560
- I don't know.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.393
(laughs)

00:01:25.393 --> 00:01:26.877
I've never used it before.

00:01:26.877 --> 00:01:28.675
- This black goes with anything.

00:01:28.675 --> 00:01:30.090
- There's gloves, your
hands are gonna get dyed.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.788
- Oh, it's for art.

00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:33.290
- You're like my competition right now,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.625
I can't tell you everything.

00:01:34.625 --> 00:01:37.583
- Oh. I'm not here to win,
I'm here to make friends.

00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:38.416
(laughs)

00:01:38.416 --> 00:01:40.810
- I am 100 percent self-taught
and I taught myself

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.016
how to make cakes from watching TV shows

00:01:43.016 --> 00:01:45.051
like Cake Boss and Ace of Cakes.

00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:48.391
I used YouTube a lot, just
kind of Googled things,

00:01:48.391 --> 00:01:52.599
and here I am, 8 years later,
and now I own a bakery.

00:01:52.599 --> 00:01:55.182
(upbeat music)

00:01:58.426 --> 00:02:00.480
- So, I'm gonna do something really crazy.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.803
- Uh oh. Are you gonna cut it?

00:02:01.803 --> 00:02:02.701
- Yes.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:06.007
I've never shaved a cake like this before.

00:02:06.007 --> 00:02:07.283
And it's really hard.

00:02:07.283 --> 00:02:08.789
- It's very risky of you to do that.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:10.746
- Yeah, I'm a risk taker.

00:02:10.746 --> 00:02:12.520
- You're a whisk taker.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.129
- A whisk taker!

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:15.419
- You're welcome.

00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:16.579
- The story of The Little Prince

00:02:16.579 --> 00:02:18.079
is this little kid that lives

00:02:18.079 --> 00:02:21.204
on a planet called Asteroid B-16,

00:02:21.204 --> 00:02:23.107
and he falls in love with a rose

00:02:23.107 --> 00:02:25.745
that grows on this planet.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:29.720
- I'm gonna take a deep breath for her,

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.530
and say a quick little prayer.

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.113
(upbeat music)

00:03:08.519 --> 00:03:09.701
- I'm really happy with it.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:12.990
I'm happy that the colors
didn't bleed together,

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.061
and that the border
stayed structurally sound,

00:03:16.061 --> 00:03:18.880
and the bow is standing
up without collapsing.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.541
- This is Asteroid B-16, which is like,

00:03:20.541 --> 00:03:22.609
16th birthday, so it makes sense.

00:03:22.609 --> 00:03:23.442
It's thematic.

00:03:23.442 --> 00:03:25.542
It was an accident, but it worked out.

00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:27.193
It was a messy process,

00:03:27.193 --> 00:03:29.670
you can see that on my
hands and the table.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.994
I think it came together pretty well.

00:03:31.994 --> 00:03:33.216
Now I guess strangers

00:03:33.216 --> 00:03:35.069
are gonna come in and judge our cakes.

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:37.156
- Do we have to be here when they judge,

00:03:37.156 --> 00:03:38.906
or can we like leave?

00:03:40.256 --> 00:03:41.541
- You know guys, I didn't
have a Sweet Sixteen,

00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:42.898
just cause I'm really bad at planning,

00:03:42.898 --> 00:03:45.955
but I would've loved for
either of these to be my cake.

00:03:45.955 --> 00:03:47.711
- This one definitely
sells the Sweet Sixteen,

00:03:47.711 --> 00:03:49.501
something about the colors
and there's a bow on top,

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.507
so it's almost like a
present and a package.

00:03:51.507 --> 00:03:53.917
This cake, I think, is
slightly cooler to me,

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:55.291
just cause it's weirder.

00:03:55.291 --> 00:03:57.347
- Is this like a Beauty
and the Beast thing?

00:03:57.347 --> 00:03:59.635
I don't really know.

00:03:59.635 --> 00:04:03.935
- I think this one
represents the theme better.

00:04:03.935 --> 00:04:05.369
- I am super impressed.

00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:07.733
I do not know who to choose.

00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:09.736
- This one, though, I have
to say is my favorite.

00:04:09.736 --> 00:04:11.628
It's a rainbow, it just looks like

00:04:11.628 --> 00:04:13.492
I want to put it in my mouth right now.

00:04:13.492 --> 00:04:14.607
- If it were my Sweet Sixteen,

00:04:14.607 --> 00:04:15.749
which I really wish it was,

00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:17.086
I would take the weird one.

00:04:17.086 --> 00:04:19.432
- For like a 16 year old girl,

00:04:19.432 --> 00:04:23.507
I would think that this
is what she would want.

00:04:23.507 --> 00:04:24.534
This is what I would want.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.622
- I like this one.

00:04:25.622 --> 00:04:27.187
- This is the cake I'd want to cut into

00:04:27.187 --> 00:04:30.191
on camera in front of all my
friends on Instagram later.

00:04:30.191 --> 00:04:32.441
(applause)

00:04:33.792 --> 00:04:36.732
- Thank you, to the people.

00:04:36.732 --> 00:04:37.565
- Congratulations.

00:04:37.565 --> 00:04:38.565
- Thank you.

00:04:39.874 --> 00:04:41.541
Well, what do I win?

00:04:42.423 --> 00:04:44.340
Yay, look at my trophy.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.501
It says, bragging rights.

00:04:48.336 --> 00:04:50.536
- The Little Prince was kind
of an obscure reference,

00:04:50.536 --> 00:04:51.924
and I kind of made it for myself,

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.237
like a selfish artist.

00:04:53.237 --> 00:04:56.739
- Oh, this is going up
on a shelf in my bakery.

00:04:56.739 --> 00:04:58.571
- Can we eat them now?

00:04:58.571 --> 00:05:01.238
(upbeat music)

